{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 3, :comments ["<b>Give ear</b>, אָרִיד — I cry out. Like it: וְהָיָה כַּאֲשֶׁר תָּרִיד (Exodus 15:14), הוֹנַח עַל הָמוֹן מִצְרִים (Exodus 15:14), and הוֹרִידֵהוּ; צָעַק אֵלָיו; וַיֵּרֶדְתִּי עַל הֶהָרִים. Although it is a different root, many are thus. And it indicates the meaning of אָרִיד, that it is like אֶזְעַק, [parallel to] the word הַקְשִׁיבָה."], :book :psalms, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 55, :notes {0 "The phrase 'ויורה על פירוש אריד שהוא כמו אזעק מלת הקשיבה' is textually awkward; translated hyper-literally. The sequence of biblical Hebrew quotations with no connectives is preserved as terse."}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Psalms -- Daat" "http://www.daat.ac.il/he-il/tanach/parshanut_hamikra/full-text/eben-ezra/tehilim"] ["Wikisource Mikraot Gedolot" "http://en.wikisource.org/wiki/Mikraot_Gedolot/"] ["Tanakh, Venice, 1617-1619" "https://dlib.rsl.ru/viewer/01007514045#?page=4"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T19:31:51.231281631Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}